Package: ttlcd-studio
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: anatolijphp <anatolijphp@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: @CORE_DEPENDS@, libgtk-3-0 | libgtk-3-0t64, libglib2.0-0 | libglib2.0-0t64, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0 | libgdk-pixbuf2.0-0, libpango-1.0-0, libcairo2, libatk1.0-0 | libatk1.0-0t64
Recommends: libayatana-appindicator3-1
Provides: ttlcd (= @VERSION@)
Conflicts: ttlcd
Replaces: ttlcd
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/anatolijphp/Thermaltake-TH240-V2-ULTRA-LCD
Description: TT LCD Studio window for the Thermaltake TH240 V2 Ultra (CL-W383) LCD
 GTK window: dashboard, live preview, display modes (image, GIF, colour,
 clock, Aura Sync, off), device and settings pages, idle picture. Complete on
 its own: it also contains everything in the ttlcd package (the ttlcd
 command, the systemd user service and the udev rule) and replaces it, so
 this one file installs from the Ubuntu App Center too.
 Bundles GTK# 3 (gtk-sharp3, LGPL-2.1) next to TTLcdStudio.exe, since Debian
 dropped that binding from its archives in 2023 (gone from Ubuntu since
 25.10); only the native GTK3/GLib/Pango/Atk/Cairo libraries above are
 needed from the system, so this installs on any current Debian/Ubuntu,
 26.04 included. See build.sh for where the bundled copy comes from.
